# Keep the monorepo build context lean (used by the repo-root Docker builds).
**/node_modules
**/.next
**/dist
**/build
**/.turbo
**/coverage
**/.terraform
**/*.tfstate*
.git
.github
**/*.log
**/.env
**/.env.local
**/.env.*.local
# Frontend is excluded from the lean backend build contexts, EXCEPT the two frontends built
# from the repo root: auth-baalvion (core-auth-baalvion) and admin-platform (admin-web, the
# admin.baalvion.com console). Re-include just those; their build artifacts stay excluded by
# the **/node_modules etc. rules below. NOTE: without admin-platform here, its source never
# enters the build context and `turbo prune baalvion-admin-platform` fails "package not found".
Frontend/*
!Frontend/auth-baalvion
!Frontend/admin-platform
# jobs.baalvion.com is built from the repo root too. Without this its source never enters
# the build context and `turbo prune baalvion-jobs-portal-web` fails "package not found" —
# which is why its image could only ever be rebuilt from a branch that was never merged.
!Frontend/Baalvion-Jobs-Portal-main
Frontend/Baalvion-Jobs-Portal-main/node_modules
Frontend/Baalvion-Jobs-Portal-main/.next
Frontend/Baalvion-Jobs-Portal-main/.turbo
# baalvion-stack (baalvionstack.com) is built from the repo root too, so its source must be
# re-included or `turbo prune baalvion-stack-web` fails with "package not found" — exactly the
# failure the note above describes.
!Frontend/baalvion-stack
Frontend/baalvion-stack/node_modules
Frontend/baalvion-stack/.next
Frontend/baalvion-stack/.turbo
# lawelitenetwork.com is built from the repo root too (its Dockerfile is monorepo-aware —
# turbo prune + pnpm — same as admin-platform), so its source must be re-included or
# `turbo prune law-elite-network-web` fails with "package not found" — exactly the failure
# the note above describes. This is the one that was actually missing: the app's own
# Dockerfile ran a bare `npm install` against workspace:* deps it could never resolve, so
# no build ever caught the missing entry here until the Dockerfile itself was fixed.
!Frontend/Law-Elite-Network-main
Frontend/Law-Elite-Network-main/node_modules
Frontend/Law-Elite-Network-main/.next
Frontend/Law-Elite-Network-main/.turbo
Frontend/auth-baalvion/node_modules
Frontend/auth-baalvion/.next
Frontend/auth-baalvion/.turbo
Frontend/admin-platform/node_modules
Frontend/admin-platform/.next
Frontend/admin-platform/.turbo
# .dockerignore matches like .gitignore -- last match wins. Every `!Frontend/X`
# re-include above re-includes X's ENTIRE tree, which silently un-excludes the
# **/.env* rules (lines 13-15) for anything under it too, since those come
# earlier in the file. Confirmed live: Frontend/Law-Elite-Network-main/.env.local
# (a real local-dev file pointing CMS_PUBLIC_URL at localhost:3018) was leaking
# into every one of these 5 apps' Docker build contexts and getting picked up
# by Next's own env loading during static generation -- baking dev URLs into
# prod ISR pages regardless of the Dockerfile's own ENV/ARG values. Re-exclude
# env files for every re-included app, the same way node_modules/.next/.turbo
# already are above.
Frontend/Law-Elite-Network-main/.env
Frontend/Law-Elite-Network-main/.env.local
Frontend/Law-Elite-Network-main/.env.*.local
Frontend/auth-baalvion/.env
Frontend/auth-baalvion/.env.local
Frontend/auth-baalvion/.env.*.local
Frontend/admin-platform/.env
Frontend/admin-platform/.env.local
Frontend/admin-platform/.env.*.local
Frontend/Baalvion-Jobs-Portal-main/.env
Frontend/Baalvion-Jobs-Portal-main/.env.local
Frontend/Baalvion-Jobs-Portal-main/.env.*.local
Frontend/baalvion-stack/.env
Frontend/baalvion-stack/.env.local
Frontend/baalvion-stack/.env.*.local
e2e
docs
*.md
# insiders directory SPA (www.marketunderworld.com), built from the repo root like the two
# above. Without this re-include its source never enters the context and `turbo prune
# investors-and-founders-web` fails "package.json not found".
!Frontend/For Invstors and Founders
Frontend/For Invstors and Founders/node_modules
Frontend/For Invstors and Founders/dist
